## llama.cpp / GGML

Nexllama links [ggml-org/llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
through the Rust crates `llama-cpp-4` / `llama-cpp-sys-4`.

- llama.cpp and GGML are licensed under the **MIT** license.
- The upstream source is vendored by `llama-cpp-sys-4` at build time; the
  resulting binary object is covered by that MIT license.
- `crates/infer-core` calls `llama_cpp_sys_4::llama_get_embeddings_seq`
  directly for rank pooling output, because the safe wrapper sizes that buffer
  incorrectly. The call is still plain llama.cpp MIT-licensed API surface.

## Runtime dependencies pulled in by the native build

Depending on the selected feature, a built backend additionally links:

- **OpenMP** (`libgomp`) — runtime exception of the GCC Runtime Library
  Exception; used by the llama.cpp CPU backend.
- **CUDA Toolkit** (`cudart`, `cublas`, ...) — NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit EULA,
  only linked when building with the `cuda` feature.
- **Vulkan** loader / LunarG SDK — Apache-2.0 (Vulkan-Loader) and the
  LunarG SDK terms, only linked when building with the `vulkan` feature.
- **Vulkan shader compiler `glslc`** — Apache-2.0, build-time only.

These are **not** redistributed in this repository. Installing the Nexllama
installer does not install any of them; a backend that needs one will simply
fail to start on a machine that lacks it.

## Rust crates

The full dependency graph with versions is in `Cargo.lock`. Licenses of every
transitive crate can be listed with:

```bash
cargo install cargo-deny && cargo deny list
```

